---
// resume.astro — the full picture. PDF pops first; scrolling reveals
// the complete expanded experience, projects, education, publications.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Resume — Dylan K. Picart">
  <section>
    <h1>Resume</h1>

    <!-- ============ Act 1: the PDF ============ -->
    <object class="resume-embed" data="/resume.pdf" type="application/pdf">
      <div class="card" style="text-align: center; padding: 3rem 1rem;">
        <p style="font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
          PDF preview isn't available on this device.
        </p>
        <a class="btn" href="/resume.pdf" download="Dylan_Picart_Data_Engineer_Resume.pdf">
          Download Resume PDF
        </a>
      </div>
    </object>

    <!-- ============ Act 2: the expanded experience ============ -->
    <h2 style="margin-top: 4.5rem;">Professional Experience</h2>
    <div class="timeline">

      <div class="tl-item reveal">
        <h3>Partnership With Children</h3>
        <p class="meta">Data Analytics &amp; Engineering Intern · Jan 2025 – Jan 2026 · NYC</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Engineered a <strong>FERPA-compliant automated ETL pipeline</strong> in Python, JavaScript, and Bash to migrate protected student records from Apricot into SharePoint, reducing a month-long manual workflow to 7 minutes while maintaining data integrity and real-time access.</li>
          <li>Developed a secure <strong>Azure-hosted Streamlit dashboard</strong> with Docker and Microsoft SSO that gave leadership reliable visibility into program performance — informing grant renewals, staffing allocation, and program expansion across NYC schools, supported by VBA automation and GitHub Actions CI/CD.</li>
          <li>Consolidated <strong>10+ years of NYSED, InfoHub, and internal program datasets</strong> using advanced SQL joins and unions, validating and reconciling discrepancies to within 0.5% margin of error and standardizing metrics supporting grant reporting and district evaluations across 30,000+ students in New York City.</li>
          <li>Migrated the entire Apricot case-management platform — 10+ years of FERPA- and HIPAA-sensitive records — into <strong>Salesforce across 32 NYC schools</strong>, partnering with non-technical stakeholders to design SOQL-driven notification Flows that fit their actual workflows, and established data governance standards adopted organization-wide.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          <span class="chip python">Python</span>
          <span class="chip js">JavaScript</span>
          <span class="chip sql">SQL</span>
          <span class="chip bash">Bash</span>
          <span class="chip">Azure</span>
          <span class="chip">Docker</span>
          <span class="chip">Streamlit</span>
          <span class="chip">Salesforce</span>
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="tl-item reveal">
        <h3>Neuromatch</h3>
        <p class="meta">NeuroAI · Computational Neuroscience · Deep Learning Researcher · Summers 2024 – 2026</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>2026 (NeuroAI):</strong> Implemented <strong>Node Perturbation learning</strong> on a multilayer perceptron for Project TardyGrad, benchmarking biologically plausible learning against Backprop and Hebbian learning on MNIST classification; NP achieved <strong>99% test accuracy on par with Backprop</strong> in the ANN setting, with degraded performance under spiking neuron conditions identifying a meaningful boundary for gradient-free learning.</li>
          <li><strong>2025 (Computational Neuroscience):</strong> Fit <strong>Generalized Linear Models to mouse visual cortex recordings</strong> spanning V1 and higher visual areas, decoding behavioral outcomes including lick and reward events and encoding neural responses to visual stimuli across learning stages, extending findings from Zhong et al. (Nature, 2025); co-authored an Impact Scholars proposal designing a temporal-difference learning extension targeting reward anticipation and prediction error signals in anterior HVAs.</li>
          <li><strong>2024 (Deep Learning):</strong> Built end-to-end pipelines in Python and Pandas to ingest, join, and transform <strong>1.5M+ COCO-MS image captions</strong>; fine-tuned and validated <strong>RoBERTa, BERT, and BLIP</strong> with PyTorch and HuggingFace, applying MLR and cosine similarity metrics to extract object-category sentiment patterns — results contributed to a peer-reviewed publication (<a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2409.09560">arXiv:2409.09560</a>).</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          <span class="chip python">Python</span>
