        <ul>
          <li>Built a production-aware <strong>RESTful API and custom SQLiteDB class</strong> with decorator-based error handling, timer logging, and input validation decorators to ingest and store NYC OpenData SARS-CoV-2 wastewater concentrations, implementing an optimized unique key extraction algorithm with <strong>O(n·m<sub>max</sub>) time complexity and O(k) space complexity</strong> for efficient JSON schema discovery across <strong>5,754 records</strong>.</li>
          <li>Applied <strong>GridSearchCV-optimized A/B testing with 5-fold cross-validation</strong> across five regression models — SGD, Polynomial, Lasso, and Random Forest — across all <strong>14 NYC wastewater facility sites</strong>, achieving <strong>R² up to 0.95</strong> and identifying consistent seasonal concentration peaks aligned with citywide COVID-19 surge patterns to support public health reporting.</li>
