          <li>Addressed significant class imbalance across adaptability levels using <strong>RandomOverSampler and RandomUnderSampler</strong> strategies, then selected the final model via A/B testing across 100 cross-validation iterations; Random Forest's <strong>F1 of 0.837</strong> outperformed KNN (0.803) and Naïve Bayes (0.685) across all three classes.</li>
